N:msad-dev-planning
D:Produces an MSAD implementation plan for a Jira epic/story/task. Reads the ticket, gathers repo context, identifies per-repo work packages, surfaces clarifying questions, writes a plan file, and hard-gates on user approval. Use when working on an MSAD feature. Don't use for one-off code edits — invoke /msad-dev-planning for any MSAD task first.
G:msad|planning|jira|epic|story|task|multi-repo|cross-repo|work-package|ddidns|zone|replication-scope|architecture-hub
U[4]:
  Planning an epic or story across the five MSAD repos
  Identifying per-repo work packages and dependencies
  Discovering related open/closed PRs to avoid duplicate work
  Getting approval before execution
S[8]{n,step}:
  1,Intake and classify the Jira ID
  2,Fetch epic/story/task and linked tickets from Jira
  3,Discover related PRs in affected repos via gh pr list
  4,Grep each repo for prior similar work and test patterns
  5,Map per-repo impact (what files change, what validators sync)
  6,Identify cross-repo dependencies (proto, error codes, validators)
  7,Surface clarifying questions and write plan file
  8,Gate on user approval (approve / approve-with-edits / reject)
R[5]:
  🔴 Cross-repo dependencies must be explicitly documented and ordered
  🔴 Windows-only code paths must note verification gate (Windows CI, not local)
  🔴 New replication-scope validators must sync across dns.config and middleware
  [ ] Plan file is written to disk and survives /clear
  [ ] User approval is mandatory before execution
F:Jira|GitHub|Atlassian MCP|gh CLI|Git|CLAUDE.md
